WEBVTT

00:07.424 --> 00:10.134
[boy breathing heavily]

00:10.135 --> 00:11.761
It'll be fine.

00:12.345 --> 00:13.929
He's gonna beat
the shit outta me.

00:13.930 --> 00:15.931
I said, it'll be fine.

00:15.932 --> 00:17.726
I'm-- I'm gonna get the belt.

00:18.351 --> 00:20.228
No, you're not.

00:20.770 --> 00:21.771
I will.

00:23.023 --> 00:24.064
[distant dog barking]

00:24.065 --> 00:25.274
[sniffling]

00:25.275 --> 00:27.402
Just go to your room,
and stay there.

00:31.322 --> 00:33.324
[footsteps receding]

00:34.868 --> 00:36.870
- [dog barking]
- [vehicle approaching]

00:50.592 --> 00:52.052
[door slamming shut]

00:57.849 --> 00:59.559
[father sighs]

01:05.607 --> 01:07.858
I'm back on patrol
in 30 minutes.

01:07.859 --> 01:10.403
So, talk fast.
What happened?

01:11.696 --> 01:13.238
You know what happened.

01:13.239 --> 01:15.033
Yeah, well,
I wanna hear it from you.

01:18.536 --> 01:20.496
I was buying pot
from this other kid.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.499
He tried to rip me off,
and we got into a fight.

01:23.792 --> 01:25.834
That's what
you're going with?

01:25.835 --> 01:27.252
- Okay.
- I'm telling the truth.

01:27.253 --> 01:29.671
No. No, you're not.

01:29.672 --> 01:31.507
I think Tommy was buying
the drugs, not you.

01:31.508 --> 01:32.674
I think you happened
to walk by,

01:32.675 --> 01:33.884
saw what was going on,

01:33.885 --> 01:36.011
- and started punching.
- Tommy didn't do anyth--

01:36.012 --> 01:37.846
I talked to the kid
you beat up, Joel,

01:37.847 --> 01:39.389
and the officers
who got called to the scene.

01:39.390 --> 01:40.600
I'm not stupid.

01:41.684 --> 01:43.268
And if you and Tommy
weren't my sons,

01:43.269 --> 01:44.854
you'd both be in juvie
right now.

01:48.066 --> 01:49.442
You're not gonna hurt him.

01:53.404 --> 01:54.489
[scoffs]

01:59.452 --> 02:01.454
- [refrigerator door opens]
- [bottles rattling]

02:09.629 --> 02:12.799
[beer cans click open]

02:18.888 --> 02:21.057
[slurping, sighs]

02:23.351 --> 02:26.980
Did I ever tell you
about that time
I stole a candy bar?

02:29.065 --> 02:30.899
I was...

02:30.900 --> 02:32.110
ten. [chuckles]

02:33.403 --> 02:35.904
Grandpa found out,
made me give it back,

02:35.905 --> 02:37.949
made me apologize
to the cashier.

02:38.950 --> 02:40.909
And then, we went home.

02:40.910 --> 02:44.414
Just before I got out
of the car, man, he just...

02:46.291 --> 02:48.250
He broke my jaw.

02:48.251 --> 02:50.752
There was blood
everywhere.

02:50.753 --> 02:52.130
Grandma thought I was dead.

02:54.465 --> 02:56.843
My mouth was wired shut
for two months.

02:58.178 --> 03:00.095
Everybody knew why.

03:00.096 --> 03:02.307
It was humiliating.

03:04.058 --> 03:06.768
If you know what it feels like,
then why?

03:06.769 --> 03:09.314
That's not why
I'm telling you this.

03:10.690 --> 03:12.400
Okay, yeah, I've hit you.

03:13.735 --> 03:14.903
And I've hit Tommy.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.282
But never like that.

03:20.283 --> 03:21.825
[choking up]
Not even close.

03:21.826 --> 03:23.786
I mean, maybe I go
too far, I...

03:25.121 --> 03:26.831
I don't know, I just...

03:27.540 --> 03:28.957
[sighs]

03:28.958 --> 03:29.959
I don't know.

03:33.880 --> 03:36.048
But I'm doing a little better
than my father did.

03:36.049 --> 03:37.050
[swallows hard]

03:42.096 --> 03:43.890
And you know,
when it's your turn...

03:47.435 --> 03:49.020
I hope you do
a little better than me.

03:52.982 --> 03:55.985
[father breathes deeply,
sniffles]

04:17.215 --> 04:21.135
[door opens, closes]

04:27.600 --> 04:30.603
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

05:25.908 --> 05:27.910
[♪ theme concludes]

05:30.038 --> 05:31.414
[bottles clinking]

05:33.291 --> 05:35.001
[patrons chattering]

05:35.960 --> 05:37.962
[door opens, closes]

05:41.591 --> 05:43.259
[knocking]

05:44.969 --> 05:47.471
Oh. The new guy.

05:47.472 --> 05:50.140
Been here two months, Seth.

05:50.141 --> 05:53.019
[Seth] Like I said.
Got somethin' for me?

05:57.190 --> 05:58.358
I'll be fucked.

05:59.692 --> 06:01.069
[toys clattering]

06:02.820 --> 06:04.863
My grandkids
are gonna love these.

06:04.864 --> 06:06.948
- How'd you find 'em?
- Searched the old homes

06:06.949 --> 06:08.493
out by Hoback.

06:09.410 --> 06:10.786
I searched those homes.

06:10.787 --> 06:12.788
Well, I know where to look
'cause I'm a smuggler,

06:12.789 --> 06:14.290
and you're a...

06:15.541 --> 06:16.918
I wasn't always this.

06:18.086 --> 06:19.253
[toy blocks thud]

06:24.342 --> 06:25.593
I was a cop.

06:26.511 --> 06:27.804
Milwaukee PD.

06:33.434 --> 06:36.396
[sniffing]
So, a trade's a trade.

06:37.105 --> 06:39.357
We can make what you want
and have it to you by, uh...

06:40.066 --> 06:41.442
Friday.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.153
No, I need it by tomorrow.

06:47.907 --> 06:50.410
Vanilla or chocolate?
Say vanilla, it's easier.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.161
Vanilla.

06:53.329 --> 06:54.747
Oh, I need one more thing.

06:55.665 --> 06:57.667
Relax.
You got a lot of 'em.

06:58.918 --> 07:01.921
[♪ light music playing]

07:39.750 --> 07:41.461
[blowing]

07:46.883 --> 07:48.885
[power tool whirring]

07:54.849 --> 07:56.851
[blowing]

07:58.853 --> 08:01.814
[♪ light music
continues playing]

08:14.494 --> 08:16.496
[♪ strumming guitar slowly]

08:22.293 --> 08:24.504
- [birds chirping]
- [distant dog barking]

08:25.463 --> 08:27.757
- [door opens]
- [Tommy] Joel!

08:32.970 --> 08:36.306
- What happened?
- Oh, where'd you come from?

08:36.307 --> 08:37.766
Painkillers, she's alright.
Come on.

08:37.767 --> 08:39.601
- [Joel] Painkillers?
- No, no, no.

08:39.602 --> 08:41.937
No, no, no, leave it.
Leave it, don't touch it.

08:41.938 --> 08:43.480
[Joel]
Tommy, what happened?

08:43.481 --> 08:45.815
She was working KP
and she burned her arm.

08:45.816 --> 08:47.026
Well, how?

08:47.693 --> 08:49.653
I pushed it
right up against a pot.

08:49.654 --> 08:51.030
You did this on purpose?

08:51.948 --> 08:54.991
I was like, "Here we go,"
and then I fucking went.

08:54.992 --> 08:58.286
- What? Why?
- No one saw.
I was on my own.

08:58.287 --> 09:00.872
And I took it off
and it was all red
and melting

09:00.873 --> 09:02.123
and gross.

09:02.124 --> 09:04.669
You know what
it smelled like?
Pork.

09:05.211 --> 09:07.379
- Who let this happen?
- What do you mean, "let"?

09:07.380 --> 09:09.714
- Who saw this comin'?
I was eating my damn dinner.
- Ow! [wincing]

09:09.715 --> 09:10.966
- Oh, it hurts.
- Okay.

09:10.967 --> 09:12.842
- Ow!
- Easy, baby girl.

09:12.843 --> 09:15.178
- Easy, easy.
- Dr. V ran over to the clinic.

09:15.179 --> 09:17.389
He's gonna come by here
with another shot.

09:17.390 --> 09:18.974
[Joel] Ellie.

09:18.975 --> 09:21.185
[Ellie breathing heavily]

09:21.894 --> 09:25.106
I just really wanted to wear
short sleeves again.

09:26.023 --> 09:28.567
I'm sorry.
I'm really sorry.

09:28.568 --> 09:30.236
[shushing]
It's okay.

09:31.737 --> 09:33.406
It's okay.
You're okay.

09:37.285 --> 09:38.578
[Joel kissing]

09:39.787 --> 09:42.707
[♪ gentle music playing]

10:03.102 --> 10:04.395
[sighs]

10:11.152 --> 10:13.529
- [Joel] Goddammit, Seth.
- Hey.

10:16.490 --> 10:17.491
Hey.

10:20.453 --> 10:23.664
"Happy 15th Birthday, Eli."

10:25.124 --> 10:26.416
[Joel groaning]

10:26.417 --> 10:28.460
Well, let's hope Seth

10:28.461 --> 10:30.379
bakes better than he spells.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.050
[mouth full]
He does.

10:35.051 --> 10:37.636
- [chuckles]
- It's really good.

10:37.637 --> 10:39.680
[Ellie laughing]

10:41.766 --> 10:45.060
Oh, right.
Uh, stay right there.

10:45.061 --> 10:47.855
I got somethin' else for you.
Close your eyes.

10:50.524 --> 10:52.234
- Keep 'em closed.
- [sighs]

10:54.737 --> 10:56.364
Okay, turn toward me.

10:59.283 --> 11:02.744
And... open.

11:02.745 --> 11:05.955
- Whoa, what's this?
- Some folks call this
a "gee-tar."

11:05.956 --> 11:07.415
[Joel chuckles]

11:07.416 --> 11:11.587
I borrowed
one of your drawings
for inspiration.

11:12.797 --> 11:16.257
Uh, took a bit of restorin'.
Real bone saddle here.

11:16.258 --> 11:18.176
Lacquered the whole body

11:18.177 --> 11:20.929
and, uh, used a Dremel
to carve the, uh--

11:20.930 --> 11:22.097
Well, that's a rotary drill.

11:22.098 --> 11:23.598
Or could be a saw,
dependin' on the tip.

11:23.599 --> 11:26.727
But, actually,
it's a pretty versatile tool.

11:30.439 --> 11:31.440
Anyway.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.151
I had promised
I would teach you, so...

11:35.152 --> 11:36.319
- Um...
- Oh.

11:36.320 --> 11:39.114
Uh, well, if you want
a lesson later...

11:39.115 --> 11:40.783
Let me hear something.

11:42.993 --> 11:45.286
- What do you mean, play it?
- And sing.

11:45.287 --> 11:47.372
No.
No, no, no, no.

11:47.373 --> 11:48.790
No, I don't sing.

11:48.791 --> 11:50.625
It's my fucking
birthday, man.

11:50.626 --> 11:52.044
Let's see what you got.

11:57.675 --> 11:58.968
Hmm.

12:03.681 --> 12:05.182
[sighs]

12:05.975 --> 12:07.977
[birds chirping]

12:11.188 --> 12:12.231
[softly] Shit.

12:15.985 --> 12:18.988
[♪ playing "Future Days"
by Pearl Jam]

12:33.127 --> 12:37.505
♪ If I ever were to lose you ♪

12:37.506 --> 12:40.634
♪ I'd surely lose myself ♪

12:42.052 --> 12:46.055
♪ Everything that
I have found dear ♪

12:46.056 --> 12:49.059
♪ I've not found by myself ♪

12:50.186 --> 12:53.606
♪ Try and sometimes
you'll succeed ♪

12:54.648 --> 12:57.526
♪ To make this man of me ♪

12:58.903 --> 13:02.697
♪ All my stolen,
missing parts ♪

13:02.698 --> 13:05.868
♪ I've no need for anymore ♪

13:07.620 --> 13:09.789
♪ I believe ♪

13:11.832 --> 13:15.920
♪ And I believe
'cause I can see ♪

13:17.087 --> 13:20.132
♪ Our future days ♪

13:21.133 --> 13:24.094
♪ Days of you and me ♪

13:24.512 --> 13:26.514
[♪ stops playing guitar]

13:29.600 --> 13:31.309
Well...

13:31.310 --> 13:33.479
- That didn't suck.
- [chuckles lightly]

13:35.856 --> 13:36.899
[Ellie lightly chuckles]

13:48.118 --> 13:49.286
[wincing]

13:53.666 --> 13:54.917
I understand.

13:57.586 --> 13:58.587
Your arm.

14:00.589 --> 14:01.757
I understand.

14:07.304 --> 14:08.806
Happy birthday, kiddo.

14:17.231 --> 14:19.275
[♪ light music playing]

14:19.984 --> 14:22.277
- [Ellie] Is it a bow and arrow?
- [Joel] Nope.

14:22.278 --> 14:24.487
[Ellie]
Is it water guns?

14:24.488 --> 14:28.032
- [Joel] No.
- Is it... a dinosaur!

14:28.033 --> 14:30.535
- You're not gonna guess.
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

14:30.536 --> 14:32.120
Is it a "lotter" of kittens?

14:32.121 --> 14:33.372
A "lotter"?

14:34.498 --> 14:35.707
You mean a litter?

14:35.708 --> 14:37.792
A litter of kittens?
Really?

14:37.793 --> 14:40.336
- Really. And no.
- Fuck.

14:40.337 --> 14:41.796
Is it a convertible?

14:41.797 --> 14:43.673
[Joel]
The hell are you gonna
do with a convertible?

14:43.674 --> 14:45.759
- [Ellie] Drive it.
- We cross here.

14:51.390 --> 14:52.808
How do you even know
where we are?

14:54.018 --> 14:56.394
I found it on patrol.

14:56.395 --> 14:59.814
You know, Jesse was 16 when
he started going on patrols.

14:59.815 --> 15:01.524
- Is that right?
- Don't get me wrong.

15:01.525 --> 15:04.652
I love counting vegetables
and shoveling sheep shit.

15:04.653 --> 15:07.030
I'm just saying, I think
I could be more useful

15:07.031 --> 15:08.197
outside the wall.

15:08.198 --> 15:10.575
You'll get on patrols
eventually.

15:10.576 --> 15:13.661
You should enjoy
being a kid for now.

15:13.662 --> 15:16.039
Oh, because childhood
has been such a joy
for me so far.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.666
You've been 16
all of four hours.

15:18.667 --> 15:20.501
We're not sending you out
until you're trained.

15:20.502 --> 15:23.171
You're gonna need
somethin' called patience.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.924
Jesse said he'd train me
if you let him.

15:26.008 --> 15:27.593
Is there somethin'
going on between you two?

15:28.802 --> 15:30.094
Excuse me?

15:30.095 --> 15:31.888
You spend a lot
of time together.

15:31.889 --> 15:33.681
- [giggling quietly]
- Is it funny?

15:33.682 --> 15:36.726
- [laughing]
- I see the way
you look at him.

15:36.727 --> 15:38.728
I got a keen eye
for these sort of things.

15:38.729 --> 15:41.606
- Uh, I don't think you do.
- Alright, none of my business.

15:41.607 --> 15:43.107
But, uh, has anyone
talked to you

15:43.108 --> 15:44.525
about the birds and the bees?

15:44.526 --> 15:46.778
Oh, you mean
dicks and vaginas?

15:46.779 --> 15:49.197
- Jesus.
- I tell you what.

15:49.198 --> 15:50.782
I promise you,
I won't get pregnant

15:50.783 --> 15:53.618
if you let me train
for patrols. Deal?

15:53.619 --> 15:56.120
I'll see what I can do.

15:56.121 --> 15:58.039
Okay, how much longer, man?

15:58.040 --> 15:59.625
[sighs]
We're here.

16:10.970 --> 16:12.220
Oh, my God.

16:12.221 --> 16:14.472
It is a dinosaur!

16:14.473 --> 16:15.807
- Joel!
- Like it?

16:15.808 --> 16:17.058
[Ellie panting]

16:17.059 --> 16:19.144
Yeah.
Likes it.

16:21.105 --> 16:23.107
[♪ gentle music playing]

16:23.691 --> 16:25.776
- [grunting]
- Whoa.

16:26.527 --> 16:28.277
Whoa, whoa.
Ellie.

16:28.278 --> 16:30.114
- [grunting]
- Ellie!

16:32.700 --> 16:35.077
Oh, my God.
Careful.

16:36.787 --> 16:40.582
I'm on a motherfucking
dinosaur! [chuckles]

16:42.668 --> 16:44.335
- Joel, there's a museum!
- Yeah, I know!

16:44.336 --> 16:46.421
If you don't fall off
the goddamn T-Rex,

16:46.422 --> 16:47.589
I'll take you there.

16:56.807 --> 16:59.518
[Ellie] [whispering]
This is so cool.

17:00.936 --> 17:03.604
How long have you known
about this place?

17:03.605 --> 17:04.981
A while.

17:04.982 --> 17:07.483
Well, then what the fuck?

17:07.484 --> 17:09.652
I was saving it
for a special day.

17:09.653 --> 17:12.697
You see?
Patience.

17:12.698 --> 17:14.575
Oh, yeah,
I've heard of that.

17:16.326 --> 17:17.327
Huh.

17:33.969 --> 17:35.971
[water dripping]

17:45.773 --> 17:47.775
[metal squeaking]

17:50.360 --> 17:51.694
It works?

17:51.695 --> 17:53.530
Somebody must have
greased it.

18:02.164 --> 18:04.208
[Ellie] Can you imagine
being up there?

18:06.835 --> 18:08.962
- Would you like to?
- Like to what?

18:09.963 --> 18:11.006
Go to space?

18:25.187 --> 18:26.187
[softly gasps]

18:26.188 --> 18:28.439
[birdsong]

18:28.440 --> 18:30.566
[Ellie] [whispering]
Is it real?

18:30.567 --> 18:33.278
It's real.
That one went up and back.

18:34.113 --> 18:36.281
Apollo 15, 1971.

18:39.076 --> 18:42.538
[♪ gentle music playing]

18:53.423 --> 18:54.675
Well, open it.

18:56.426 --> 18:58.428
[Joel chuckles]

19:01.932 --> 19:04.475
[metal door creaking]

19:04.476 --> 19:06.353
- [whispering] You got it.
- [Ellie sighs]

19:08.772 --> 19:10.064
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

19:10.065 --> 19:12.066
You're going up to space.

19:12.067 --> 19:13.402
You need a helmet.

19:16.738 --> 19:18.157
[grunting]

19:21.410 --> 19:22.578
Pick one.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.515
[glass shattering]

19:56.737 --> 19:59.740
[♪ gentle music playing]

20:04.203 --> 20:06.162
How's it smell in there?

20:06.163 --> 20:09.040
Like space, and dust.

20:09.041 --> 20:11.293
Well, good.
Then, you're ready.

20:25.724 --> 20:27.559
[grunting]

20:32.189 --> 20:33.273
[hatch door thuds]

20:34.483 --> 20:36.734
[Ellie imitating lasers firing]

20:36.735 --> 20:38.654
[imitating static]

20:39.363 --> 20:42.490
People of Discovery, set!
Abort!

20:42.491 --> 20:44.534
[switches clicking]

20:47.788 --> 20:49.623
They sat right here.

20:52.000 --> 20:53.210
[Ellie chuckles]

20:54.336 --> 20:57.380
- Happy birthday, kiddo.
- What's this?

20:57.381 --> 21:02.009
This is something that took
a mighty effort to find.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.178
Play it.

21:13.397 --> 21:14.523
[seat creaking]

21:19.987 --> 21:21.862
Close your eyes.

21:21.863 --> 21:23.490
It'll be worth it.

21:25.993 --> 21:27.160
[Walkman clicking]

21:28.787 --> 21:31.622
[NASA Public Affairs Officer]
Thirty seconds and counting.

21:31.623 --> 21:33.541
Astronauts report
it feels good.

21:33.542 --> 21:35.335
T-minus 25 seconds.

21:38.547 --> 21:40.173
Twenty seconds and counting.

21:42.342 --> 21:45.803
T-minus 15 seconds.
Guidance is internal.

21:45.804 --> 21:49.724
Twelve, eleven, ten, nine.

21:49.725 --> 21:51.559
Ignition sequence starts.

21:51.560 --> 21:52.810
[spacecraft whooshing,
rattling]

21:52.811 --> 21:56.230
Six, five, four, three,

21:56.231 --> 21:58.899
two, one, zero.

21:58.900 --> 22:01.569
- [rockets booming]
- All engines running.

22:01.570 --> 22:03.738
Liftoff!
We have a liftoff,

22:03.739 --> 22:07.492
32 minutes past the hour,
liftoff on Apollo 11.

22:13.040 --> 22:15.042
[rattling and booming
decreasing]

22:16.626 --> 22:19.629
[♪ gentle music playing]

22:46.114 --> 22:48.116
[birdsong]

22:50.160 --> 22:52.119
I do okay?

22:52.120 --> 22:53.622
Are you kidding me?

22:56.416 --> 22:58.418
[both laughing]

23:01.213 --> 23:02.506
[Ellie sighs]

23:16.853 --> 23:18.146
This is nice.

23:19.773 --> 23:22.609
- We should do this more.
- Yeah. In.

23:33.620 --> 23:34.996
You okay?

23:36.540 --> 23:37.624
Yeah.

23:56.601 --> 23:58.603
[rain pattering]

24:13.660 --> 24:15.662
[rain continues]

24:23.753 --> 24:26.922
[Ellie] [giggling, muffled]
Stop.

24:26.923 --> 24:28.967
[people laughing]

24:31.511 --> 24:33.721
[laughter continues]

24:33.722 --> 24:35.182
- [banging]
- [Ellie] Fuck.

24:37.058 --> 24:38.560
Joel, what the fuck?

24:39.436 --> 24:41.228
Exactly.
What the fuck?

24:41.229 --> 24:43.147
- Get outta here.
- No, wait.

24:43.148 --> 24:44.732
What-- what are you
even doing here?

24:44.733 --> 24:46.150
You're supposed to be
on patrol.

24:46.151 --> 24:49.236
I came home early to...
surprise you for your birthday.

24:49.237 --> 24:51.948
- [Ellie] [whispering] Oh, yeah.
- Seventeen, by the way.

24:52.532 --> 24:54.409
Well, I'm 19, so...

24:55.785 --> 24:57.454
I'm gonna go.

24:59.998 --> 25:02.375
- Fuck is that?
- Fuck.

25:05.337 --> 25:07.421
It's not done yet,
it's gonna look better
when I fill in--

25:07.422 --> 25:08.715
- [Joel] Leave.
- Right.

25:12.093 --> 25:13.136
[Ellie sighing]

25:19.309 --> 25:21.520
So, all the teenage shit
all at once, huh?

25:22.854 --> 25:26.066
Drugs, and tattoos, and sex.

25:26.608 --> 25:29.319
Experimenting with, uh, with--
[stammering] with girls?

25:30.529 --> 25:33.740
It wasn't sex, and it
wasn't a fucking experiment.

25:36.743 --> 25:38.203
You don't know
what you're sayin'.

25:39.955 --> 25:41.915
We'll discuss this later,
when you're yourself.

25:44.084 --> 25:45.544
- [door slamming]
- [sighs]

25:46.795 --> 25:48.797
[thunder rumbling]

25:55.637 --> 25:57.639
[rain falling]

26:01.059 --> 26:03.061
[thunder continues rumbling]

26:09.025 --> 26:11.027
[rain pattering]

26:17.534 --> 26:19.536
[heavy thudding]

26:27.377 --> 26:29.379
[Ellie grunting]

26:33.008 --> 26:35.426
- The hell are you doing?
- Moving into the garage.

26:35.427 --> 26:37.596
The hell you are.
Ellie, let go.

26:38.305 --> 26:40.180
It's the middle of the night.
It's pissin' rain out there.

26:40.181 --> 26:41.890
Now, get this back on the bed.

26:41.891 --> 26:43.767
There's no heat
or running water in the garage.

26:43.768 --> 26:45.979
- You can't stay there.
- Okay, fine.

26:47.439 --> 26:49.566
Okay, you want to have
this conversation? Fine.

26:50.692 --> 26:52.610
You may not like the rules,
but this is my house.

26:52.611 --> 26:55.070
No, it isn't.
You don't own it.

26:55.071 --> 26:58.240
They gave it to you.
Sorry, to us.

26:58.241 --> 26:59.993
You don't own anything.

27:01.077 --> 27:03.079
[rain continues pattering]

27:11.171 --> 27:13.297
Look, I'm s-sorry
that I got a tattoo,

27:13.298 --> 27:16.259
and smoked weed,
and fooled around with a girl.

27:18.345 --> 27:19.679
Except, I'm not.

27:22.724 --> 27:23.850
Maybe, um...

27:28.271 --> 27:30.440
Maybe it's a good thing
for you to have
your own space.

27:32.984 --> 27:34.485
Just give me a few days

27:34.486 --> 27:36.363
and let me fix things up
a little out there.

27:38.573 --> 27:39.574
Okay.

27:43.453 --> 27:44.454
Come on.

28:00.970 --> 28:02.513
[sighs] Thanks.

28:02.514 --> 28:03.556
Sure.

28:06.976 --> 28:08.144
Can I see?

28:14.526 --> 28:16.528
- Did it hurt?
- Yeah.

28:19.072 --> 28:20.490
But kinda good.

28:24.202 --> 28:25.704
It's actually not bad.

28:27.038 --> 28:31.334
Better than the,
uh, one I made
on your guitar anyway.

28:37.465 --> 28:39.300
I never did ask.
What is it with the moths?

28:41.511 --> 28:43.679
Um, nothing. Just--

28:43.680 --> 28:47.224
I just read about them
in a book on dreams and stuff.

28:47.225 --> 28:48.976
It's kind of symbolic.

28:48.977 --> 28:50.395
Oh, right.

28:52.439 --> 28:57.360
Yeah, like change and--
and growin' and such.

29:01.322 --> 29:02.490
It's late.

29:03.283 --> 29:04.284
Yeah.

29:05.994 --> 29:07.078
Well, good night.

29:08.329 --> 29:09.330
Night.

29:12.083 --> 29:13.960
[door creaking]

29:18.923 --> 29:20.925
- [door opens]
- [people chattering]

29:24.596 --> 29:26.598
[door closes]

29:28.475 --> 29:29.517
[Joel] Hey.

29:32.270 --> 29:35.940
You guys study, uh,
dreams and stuff, right?

29:37.317 --> 29:39.526
Is there
a "Doctor Is In" sign
on me like Lucy

29:39.527 --> 29:41.446
from fuckin' Peanuts?

29:44.407 --> 29:47.868
Yes, some doctors
studied dreams.

29:47.869 --> 29:49.912
The dumb ones, mostly.

29:49.913 --> 29:51.122
So, a moth.

29:52.207 --> 29:55.918
That probably means
change and-- and growth?

29:55.919 --> 29:57.629
No, that would be
a butterfly.

29:58.671 --> 30:00.881
Oh.
So, what's a moth?

30:00.882 --> 30:02.050
Death.

30:03.384 --> 30:04.928
If you believe in that shit.

30:14.813 --> 30:15.814
Why?

30:23.029 --> 30:25.031
[footsteps receding]

30:27.158 --> 30:28.701
[door opens]

30:30.036 --> 30:31.662
[door closes]

30:31.663 --> 30:34.707
[♪ soft music playing]

30:45.552 --> 30:47.554
[poster rustling]

31:19.085 --> 31:21.462
Okay,
so I've been thinking...

31:22.589 --> 31:25.132
or wondering--
no, thinking,

31:25.133 --> 31:27.093
uh, for a while now...

31:28.094 --> 31:30.263
about Salt Lake City.

31:32.015 --> 31:33.808
I just want
to understand it.

31:35.810 --> 31:38.563
So, I wrote down
some questions.

31:39.856 --> 31:40.857
Okay?

31:43.276 --> 31:44.277
Okay.

31:53.202 --> 31:55.871
One, if the Fireflies

31:55.872 --> 31:58.415
spotted us a mile
from the hospital,

31:58.416 --> 32:01.502
how did they get surprised
by an entire group of Raiders?

32:05.423 --> 32:07.049
Two.

32:07.050 --> 32:10.344
If the Raiders could
kill all those soldiers,

32:10.345 --> 32:14.222
and Marlene, and you had
to carry me the whole time,

32:14.223 --> 32:15.683
how did we get away?

32:17.268 --> 32:19.686
Three, if there are dozens
of immune people,

32:19.687 --> 32:21.648
- why hasn't anyone heard--
- [knocking]

32:22.690 --> 32:23.941
[knocking]

32:23.942 --> 32:24.984
[Joel] Ellie?

32:26.611 --> 32:27.862
Uh, coming.

32:32.408 --> 32:34.494
- [clearing throat]
- Whoa.

32:35.328 --> 32:37.204
Already dressed.

32:37.205 --> 32:39.039
I figured
I'd be waking you up.

32:39.040 --> 32:41.541
Uh, nope.
I had trouble sleeping.

32:41.542 --> 32:42.709
Huh.

32:42.710 --> 32:44.211
Well, guess what?
That works out great

32:44.212 --> 32:45.879
for your birthday present.

32:45.880 --> 32:48.299
You're 19
and you've been patient.

32:49.467 --> 32:51.385
So, I told 'em
I was okay with it.

32:51.386 --> 32:54.389
- With what?
- Your first patrol.

32:56.766 --> 32:58.559
- I'll grab my coat.
- And a gun.

33:04.941 --> 33:07.484
[crow cawing]

33:07.485 --> 33:09.529
[horse chortling]

33:11.030 --> 33:12.906
[Ellie]
So, what's the record
for number of kills

33:12.907 --> 33:14.616
on a training run?

33:14.617 --> 33:17.661
Zero. This is
the safest trail we got.

33:17.662 --> 33:18.912
Gotta start easy.

33:18.913 --> 33:20.873
Ah, great.
Happy birthday to me.

33:22.083 --> 33:24.960
- Come on, binoculars.
- Why? There's nothing out here.

33:24.961 --> 33:27.338
I know, but this is about
learnin' the ropes.

33:28.256 --> 33:30.049
So, pretend, okay?

33:32.343 --> 33:34.928
It's part of the rules.
You stick with your partner,

33:34.929 --> 33:37.557
scan the countryside,
be ready for anything.

33:38.099 --> 33:39.475
- Oh, shit.
- What?

33:41.227 --> 33:43.938
There's a little squirrel
fucking a big squirrel!

33:44.856 --> 33:46.149
We should probably
report that.

33:48.609 --> 33:50.278
Fine, we'll skip
the scannin' for now.

33:54.949 --> 33:56.950
But this is nice, right?

33:56.951 --> 33:59.912
Reminds me of the old days,
just you and me on the trail.

34:00.997 --> 34:02.956
I know you got stuff going on,
but it'd be nice

34:02.957 --> 34:05.542
if we could do
this kind of thing more often.

34:05.543 --> 34:06.794
Spend time together.

34:10.089 --> 34:11.090
Yeah.

34:15.803 --> 34:17.804
- You okay?
- Yeah.

34:17.805 --> 34:19.473
- It's just, you look...
- No, I--

34:19.474 --> 34:21.349
- There's nothin' on your mind?
- No, nothing.

34:21.350 --> 34:23.436
[dispatcher] [over radio]
Cache Creek, this is Jackson.
Come in.

34:26.898 --> 34:29.733
- Go for Cache Creek.
- Infected north of Pinnacle.

34:29.734 --> 34:32.652
Eugene and Adam need backup.
You're the closest we've got.

34:32.653 --> 34:34.696
- [horse chortling]
- I'll be there in ten.

34:34.697 --> 34:36.323
Tell them to dig in.

34:36.324 --> 34:37.699
- Go back to Jackson.
- No.

34:37.700 --> 34:39.534
Ellie, it's not safe.
Go back.

34:39.535 --> 34:41.161
I'm not your fucking kid,
Joel.

34:41.162 --> 34:43.289
I'm your partner.
We stick together.

34:46.876 --> 34:48.835
[horse neighing]

34:48.836 --> 34:50.296
[Joel clicking tongue]

34:53.424 --> 34:56.427
[♪ ominous music playing]

35:16.364 --> 35:19.158
We'll hike down from here.
Faster than the switchback.

35:34.257 --> 35:37.260
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

35:51.482 --> 35:53.943
- [distant screeching]
- [distant gunshot]

35:56.487 --> 35:58.238
You remember
what I taught you?

35:58.239 --> 35:59.782
I'm your back.
You're mine.

36:07.915 --> 36:09.917
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

36:23.472 --> 36:24.682
[mysterious noise approaching]

36:28.686 --> 36:30.688
[horse whinnying]

36:35.735 --> 36:36.861
Come on.

36:40.865 --> 36:42.867
[leaves crunching]

36:45.828 --> 36:48.331
♪

37:05.139 --> 37:06.557
Oh, shit.
Eugene.

37:07.308 --> 37:08.309
[Joel] Ellie.

37:13.397 --> 37:14.648
You clean?

37:14.649 --> 37:15.650
Uh...

37:17.318 --> 37:18.402
Uh...

37:19.487 --> 37:20.488
No.

37:25.117 --> 37:26.743
- Are there any more?
- Joel.

37:26.744 --> 37:28.663
Are there any more?

37:29.413 --> 37:30.873
Other than me?

37:34.377 --> 37:35.378
No.

37:37.546 --> 37:40.340
- Whoa.
- Okay, okay. Look.

37:40.341 --> 37:43.343
Please, I-- I-- I figure
I got about an hour.

37:43.344 --> 37:46.012
So, this is what we do.
We go back to the gate.

37:46.013 --> 37:48.348
They let Gail out,

37:48.349 --> 37:50.517
keeping her
at a safe distance,
of course.

37:50.518 --> 37:52.728
And I-- I say...

37:53.854 --> 37:55.064
goodbye.

37:56.691 --> 37:57.858
We can't do that.

37:58.859 --> 38:00.486
Yes-- yes, we can.

38:05.116 --> 38:08.077
- Yes, we can.
- You're empty.

38:10.246 --> 38:11.247
[groaning]

38:12.456 --> 38:13.832
No. [stammering]

38:13.833 --> 38:16.543
Joel, I gotta go back.
I gotta see her.

38:16.544 --> 38:20.089
I got things
I gotta tell her.

38:22.842 --> 38:24.426
Things.

38:24.427 --> 38:26.512
- You don't understand.
- I do.

38:27.513 --> 38:29.597
But we have rules,
and it can't happen.

38:29.598 --> 38:30.641
Wait.

38:34.270 --> 38:35.729
- Whoa.
- Hold out your hand.

38:35.730 --> 38:36.772
Huh?

38:41.819 --> 38:42.987
Hold out your hand.

38:46.198 --> 38:49.452
Now, count slowly,
clearly, from one to ten.

38:51.662 --> 38:54.914
One, two, three,

38:54.915 --> 38:56.916
four, five,

38:56.917 --> 39:00.253
six, seven, eight,

39:00.254 --> 39:02.840
nine, ten.

39:03.841 --> 39:05.300
He has time.

39:05.301 --> 39:07.178
We tie him up
and we bring him back.

39:09.638 --> 39:11.640
Joel, let him see
his fucking wife.

39:12.933 --> 39:14.268
Please.

39:15.811 --> 39:17.103
[sighs]

39:17.104 --> 39:19.315
[breathing heavily]

39:22.109 --> 39:24.152
Get the horses,
bring them down the trail.

39:24.153 --> 39:26.155
I'll start walkin' with him,
we'll meet up with you.

39:39.585 --> 39:40.669
I promise.

39:50.763 --> 39:52.181
Go ahead, ten feet.

39:53.265 --> 39:54.266
Thank you.

40:06.195 --> 40:08.197
[foliage rustling]

40:18.749 --> 40:20.751
[Eugene panting]

40:21.752 --> 40:24.922
It makes you cold.
The Cordyceps.

40:26.507 --> 40:28.342
I didn't expect that.

40:32.263 --> 40:35.683
[sighs]
Which, uh, way?

40:39.186 --> 40:40.271
Head right.

40:44.275 --> 40:46.277
[Eugene shivering]

40:59.957 --> 41:01.876
It's beautiful.

41:04.336 --> 41:06.839
[♪ ominous music playing]

41:08.632 --> 41:09.633
Oh.

41:11.927 --> 41:14.138
I need you
to not turn around.

41:15.306 --> 41:16.931
No.

41:16.932 --> 41:18.433
Uh, you can't--

41:18.434 --> 41:20.393
you can't do this to me.

41:20.394 --> 41:22.645
Joel.

41:22.646 --> 41:25.398
If you have last words for her,
I'll pass them along.

41:25.399 --> 41:27.067
[Eugene]
Last words for her?

41:28.027 --> 41:31.572
No, no, I need--
I need her last words!

41:32.698 --> 41:34.116
For me!

41:36.619 --> 41:37.912
I'm dying.

41:39.038 --> 41:40.998
I'm terrified.
I, uh...

41:46.587 --> 41:47.880
I don't need a view.

41:51.300 --> 41:52.676
I need Gail.

41:55.304 --> 41:57.348
To see her face.
Please.

41:58.516 --> 42:00.851
Please let that be
the last thing I see.

42:06.524 --> 42:07.983
If you love someone...

42:10.986 --> 42:12.571
you can always see their face.

42:15.157 --> 42:18.369
[♪ somber music playing]

42:20.538 --> 42:22.039
[sighs]

42:30.881 --> 42:33.884
♪

42:49.900 --> 42:51.193
I see her.

42:53.571 --> 42:56.574
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

43:14.967 --> 43:16.969
[foliage rustling]

43:18.012 --> 43:20.014
[hoofbeats]

43:45.247 --> 43:46.415
I'm sorry.

44:08.604 --> 44:10.814
I'm gonna radio ahead
and let them know.

44:12.941 --> 44:17.487
When we get there,
I'll-- I'll tell Gail

44:17.488 --> 44:19.907
what she needs to know,
and nothin' more.

44:21.450 --> 44:22.868
It's the right thing to do.

44:26.580 --> 44:27.581
Ellie.

44:32.127 --> 44:33.545
I had no choice.

44:53.273 --> 44:55.275
[crow cawing]

45:14.962 --> 45:18.090
Uh, he was bit
when we found him.

45:19.800 --> 45:20.926
And, uh...

45:22.761 --> 45:24.847
Well, he wanted to tell you
that he loved you.

45:28.600 --> 45:32.061
And, uh, he wished
he could say goodbye
to you in person

45:32.062 --> 45:34.063
but he didn't wanna
put you in danger.

45:34.064 --> 45:35.566
[crying] No, no.

45:36.191 --> 45:38.694
[Joel]
And he wasn't scared. He...

45:39.737 --> 45:41.155
He was brave.

45:44.366 --> 45:45.992
And he ended it himself.

45:45.993 --> 45:47.536
[sighs]

45:50.873 --> 45:52.875
[sobbing]

45:59.381 --> 46:00.799
[Ellie]
That's not what happened.

46:06.764 --> 46:09.558
He begged to see you.
He had time.

46:10.267 --> 46:12.727
Joel promised
to take him to you.

46:12.728 --> 46:14.271
He promised us both.

46:17.232 --> 46:20.068
[softly] And then,
Joel shot him in the head.

46:24.448 --> 46:26.450
[breathing heavily]

46:30.788 --> 46:31.955
That's...

46:35.334 --> 46:37.627
Get away. Please.

46:37.628 --> 46:39.671
Get away from me, please.

46:46.094 --> 46:47.429
You swore.

46:49.932 --> 46:51.767
[Gail sobbing]

46:55.395 --> 46:57.356
[Gail] [sobbing] No.

47:12.830 --> 47:15.833
[♪ "Little Sadie"
by Crooked Still playing]

47:17.334 --> 47:19.418
♪ Standing on the corner
reading a bill ♪

47:19.419 --> 47:21.254
♪ And up stepped
the sheriff from Thomasville ♪

47:21.255 --> 47:23.506
♪ He said,
"Miss, is your name Brown? ♪

47:23.507 --> 47:27.094
♪ Remember the night
you shot Sadie down?" ♪

47:28.262 --> 47:31.639
♪ I said, oh yes, sir,
but my name is Lee ♪

47:31.640 --> 47:33.683
♪ And I murdered Little Sadie
in the first degree ♪

47:33.684 --> 47:35.810
♪ First degree
and second degree ♪

47:35.811 --> 47:40.107
♪ Got any papers,
will you read 'em to me? ♪

47:46.905 --> 47:48.489
- [♪ song ends]
- [Dina laughing]

47:48.490 --> 47:49.949
That was good, yeah?

47:49.950 --> 47:51.285
[people cheering]

47:51.660 --> 47:53.119
Oh, okay.

47:53.120 --> 47:55.538
Yeah, he's fallin' apart.
I'm gonna get him to bed.

47:55.539 --> 47:58.165
- You're gonna miss
the countdown.
- I'll come back after.

47:58.166 --> 48:00.126
[singer]
Okay. The next one
is a little slower.

48:00.127 --> 48:01.836
Save me some of that.

48:01.837 --> 48:03.129
Say goodnight
to Uncle Grumpy.

48:03.130 --> 48:05.840
- Goodnight, Uncle Grumpy.
- [Tommy chuckles]

48:05.841 --> 48:08.467
- Night, kiddo.
- See you next year.

48:08.468 --> 48:10.636
See you next year.

48:10.637 --> 48:13.640
[♪ "Ecstasy"
by Crooked Still playing]

48:20.814 --> 48:22.649
- [Maria] You okay?
- Hm?

48:24.151 --> 48:25.319
Yeah, I'm fine.

48:27.237 --> 48:29.989
What I said today
about you being a refugee

48:29.990 --> 48:31.991
probably came off
as ungrateful.

48:31.992 --> 48:34.995
- No, it's okay.
- Well, I am grateful.

48:35.913 --> 48:38.205
You mean a lot to us.
To all of us.

48:38.206 --> 48:40.374
But especially to me
and Tommy.

48:40.375 --> 48:44.171
What I'm trying to say is,
Uncle Grumpy is family.

48:45.255 --> 48:47.882
And family
helps each other out,

48:47.883 --> 48:49.342
if you need it.

48:49.343 --> 48:52.345
♪ Oh, when shall I see
Jesus and reign... ♪

48:52.346 --> 48:54.556
Hey, it's a family event.

48:55.849 --> 48:56.850
Sorry.

48:59.019 --> 49:00.728
Sorry.

49:00.729 --> 49:03.105
In a church.
Dykes.

49:03.106 --> 49:04.732
- [Ellie] Fuck did you just say?
- [Dina] Ellie, no.

49:04.733 --> 49:05.859
Ellie, hey. No.

49:06.693 --> 49:07.902
[crowd gasping]

49:07.903 --> 49:09.488
You get the hell out of here.

49:10.197 --> 49:11.864
[Maria]
Seth. Let's...

49:11.865 --> 49:14.951
- [Seth grunting]
- Let's take a walk.

49:14.952 --> 49:16.703
Come on.
Let's go.

49:19.039 --> 49:20.082
Are you okay?

49:21.416 --> 49:22.876
What is wrong with you?

49:26.755 --> 49:29.424
I don't need
your fucking help.

49:37.975 --> 49:38.976
Right.

49:43.397 --> 49:46.400
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

50:07.337 --> 50:09.339
[♪ strums guitar]

50:10.799 --> 50:12.801
♪

50:23.979 --> 50:25.981
[♪ guitar continues
playing faintly]

50:30.694 --> 50:31.820
[♪ stops playing]

51:44.559 --> 51:45.811
What are you drinking?

51:47.771 --> 51:48.772
Coffee.

51:49.773 --> 51:51.900
- Where'd you get it?
- Um...

51:53.151 --> 51:55.402
[smacks lips]
The people that
came through last week.

51:55.403 --> 51:57.947
- Mm.
- I'm a little embarrassed

51:57.948 --> 52:00.075
for what I traded
to get it, but...

52:01.326 --> 52:02.786
it's not bad.

52:13.213 --> 52:14.840
I had Seth under control.

52:17.551 --> 52:19.718
Yeah, I know.

52:19.719 --> 52:22.597
And I don't wanna ever
hear about you taking me
off patrol again.

52:25.267 --> 52:26.268
Okay.

52:34.025 --> 52:35.402
So, Dina.

52:38.029 --> 52:40.322
Is she your girlfriend now?

52:40.323 --> 52:42.659
No. No, she...

52:44.828 --> 52:47.747
It was just one kiss.
Didn't mean anything.

52:50.167 --> 52:51.668
I don't know
why she did that.

52:54.212 --> 52:55.213
But...

52:57.090 --> 52:58.216
you do like her?

53:02.262 --> 53:04.723
[sighs]
I'm so stupid.

53:08.393 --> 53:11.354
Look, I don't know what
Dina's intentions are, but...

53:15.275 --> 53:16.902
well, she'd be lucky
to have you.

53:20.572 --> 53:22.199
You're such an asshole.

53:27.704 --> 53:28.997
You lied to me.

53:30.790 --> 53:33.375
You looked me in the eyes
and you lied,

53:33.376 --> 53:35.170
and it was the same face.

53:36.421 --> 53:38.548
Same fucking look.

53:43.178 --> 53:44.804
But I think I knew already.

53:47.515 --> 53:49.226
I knew this whole time.

53:55.732 --> 53:57.651
So, I'm gonna give you
one last chance.

54:00.028 --> 54:02.030
Tell me what happened
with the Fireflies.

54:03.615 --> 54:06.493
If you lie to me again,
we're done.

54:16.586 --> 54:18.088
Were there other
immune people?

54:33.937 --> 54:35.522
Were there Raiders?

54:45.031 --> 54:46.616
Could they have made a cure?

55:03.466 --> 55:04.467
[sniffling]

55:08.305 --> 55:09.597
Did you--

55:16.187 --> 55:17.647
And Marlene?

55:24.738 --> 55:26.031
[sighs]

55:27.198 --> 55:28.450
Making a cure...

55:31.369 --> 55:32.620
would've killed you.

55:34.331 --> 55:36.248
Then, I was supposed to die.

55:36.249 --> 55:37.583
[sniffling]
That was my purpose.

55:37.584 --> 55:39.168
My life would have
fucking mattered!

55:39.169 --> 55:40.837
But you took that from me!

55:41.838 --> 55:43.548
You took it from everyone.

55:45.675 --> 55:46.676
Yes.

55:47.510 --> 55:48.511
[sighs]

55:49.971 --> 55:51.431
And I'll pay the price...

55:53.016 --> 55:55.143
because you're gonna
turn away from me.

55:56.227 --> 55:58.438
[breathing heavily]

56:00.148 --> 56:03.026
But if somehow I
had a second chance
at that moment...

56:06.988 --> 56:08.448
I would do it all over again.

56:11.701 --> 56:13.578
Because you're selfish.

56:14.871 --> 56:16.373
[choking up]
Because I love you.

56:21.795 --> 56:23.797
[whimpers]
In a way you...

56:25.632 --> 56:27.759
you can't understand.

56:30.678 --> 56:31.971
Maybe you never will.

56:35.475 --> 56:37.227
But if that day should come...

56:40.021 --> 56:42.065
if you should ever
have one of your own...

56:48.655 --> 56:49.739
well, then...

56:54.035 --> 56:55.870
I hope you do
a little better than me.

56:56.996 --> 56:58.081
[Ellie sniffling]

57:02.794 --> 57:05.088
[sighs deeply]

57:13.471 --> 57:15.890
I don't think I can
forgive you for this.

57:25.567 --> 57:27.277
But I would like to try.

57:30.822 --> 57:33.825
[♪ gentle music playing]

57:40.081 --> 57:42.083
[rain falling]

57:44.752 --> 57:46.838
[thunder rumbling]

57:56.806 --> 57:58.891
[thunder crashing]

57:58.892 --> 58:01.895
[♪ soft music playing]

58:07.859 --> 58:10.278
[♪ music swells]

58:14.073 --> 58:17.076
[♪ gentle music playing]

59:24.143 --> 59:26.062
[♪ music fades out]
